<SCENARIO VER="105">
<TXSPN>Against my will, a scenario like that appeared. 
{PAUSE ""}
This is the first time my control has failed in this world.<PG>
No, now that I think about it... 
{PAUSE ""}
A few times, against my will, there were several scenes that made no sense, were there not? 
{PAUSE ""}
Do you remember?<PG>
For example, in the last scenario of the Meicho Arc, my father, Eiichiro Niimura, who should have been dead, appeared―<PG>
At the end of the Jusatsu Arc's 'Infection,' even Erina Goto awakened to precognition―<PG>
In the Shigatsu Arc's 'I Came to See You.', Sakura Niimura, who should have been dead, appeared before Erina Goto―<PG>
Like this, endings I did not foresee occurred, and I answered on the spot, '<VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama has no need to know,' but...<PG>
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\イラスト\立木\春花用立ち絵\春花悲しい.lcm" "REPEAT" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
Somehow, I knew. 
{PAUSE ""}
That in <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama, the will to know the truth was steadily welling up.<PG>
That in answer to that will, this world had begun, little by little, to change its shape.<PG>
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\イラスト\立木\春花用立ち絵\春花通常.lcm" "REPEAT" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
I believe it is surely <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama's desire to know the truth that is moving this world. 
{PAUSE ""}
This world is becoming a world that reflects not only my will, but <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama's will as well.<PG>
And that will has even dragged into the light the fact I kept hiding: 'I stabbed Natsumi to death.'<PG>
It seems this world changes its shape at the slightest thing.
{PAUSE ""}
{}
<EVENT VALUE="NOREPAGE">
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
